# Build-context hygiene for the root Dockerfile (all targets).

# VCS, tooling output, per-language caches, runtime upload artifacts (the ETL
# volume starts empty instead of being seeded with dev leftovers)
.git
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.dev-session
**/uploads

# Secrets: .env.keys only ever enters a build as a BuildKit secret (never a
# layer) and plaintext `**/.env` files don't belong inside an image — compose
# bind-mounts the encrypted root `.env.prod` + `.env.keys` read-only at runtime
# instead (the etl stage decrypts them in-process via app/core/env.py). The
# encrypted `.env.local` / `.env.prod` deliberately STAY in the context: the
# build scripts decrypt them.
.env.keys
**/.env.keys
**/.env

# The canonical bake of the host's decrypted local env must never ship — the
# backend stage re-bakes it under dotenvx during its own build step, and the
# postinstall stub covers everything else.
**/src/generated/runtime-env.ts
